on":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- 4.x as far as I know => introduced in [this commit](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/7961a1dea3e7ce8c4e7197a0000e35ab31e9ff2e) / [this PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/45845)\n\n### System information\n\nN/A\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen instantiating a Range element in GDScript, the default value for the step is 1.0 instead of 0.01 as stated in the documentation.\n- In the C++ class (scene/gui/range.h - line 42), the value is initialized as:\n  - `double step = 1.0;`\n- The documentation (doc/classes/Range.xml - line 66) defines it as follows:\n  - `<member name=\"step\" type=\"float\" setter=\"set_step\" getter=\"get_step\" default=\"0.01\">`\n\nAs such, when creating the node within the editor, the documentation value (0.01) is properly assigned.\nHowever, when creating the node from the code instead, the C++ value (1.0) is assigned.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a scene with any node at the root\n- Attach a script to the node and copy/paste the following code inside:\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar range_test := Range.new()\n\tprint(range_test.step)\n```\n- Launch the scene and check the Console's output (should display 1.0 instead of 0.01)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A (check provided code snippet)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https